## Components of Dataset

Within a dataset there are different **TERMS** for for each part of the dataset, e.g. the rows, columns and values.

::::: columns
::: {.column width="50%"}
-   Each **COLUMN** is a **VARIABLE**.

-   **COLUMN LABELS** are **VARIABLE NAMES**.

-   Each **ROW**is an **OBSERVATION**.

-   Individual **CELLS (VALUES)** are **DATA** or **DATA VALUES**.
:::

::: {.column width="50%"}
```{r echo=F}

gt_cars <- gtcars |>
  rownames_to_column(var="Obs") |>
  mutate(Num_Gears=substr(trsmn,1,1) |> factor(),
         Transmission=substr(trsmn,2,3),
         Obs=as.integer(Obs)) |>
  select(1:3,6,11,17) |>
  filter(!mfr=="Tesla" | mfr=="Acura") |>
  rename("Obs_No"="Obs", "Manufacturer"="mfr", 
         "Model"="model", "Body_Style"="bdy_style", "City_MPG"="mpg_c") |> 
  select(Obs_No:Body_Style, Num_Gears, City_MPG) 

 gt_tabl1 <- gt_cars[1:10,] |> kable(align=c("c","l","l","l","c","c"), escape = F) |>
  row_spec(0, bold=T, background="lavender", color="black") |>
  column_spec(2, bold=T, background="yellow", color="black") |>
  row_spec(5, bold=T, background="tomato", color="black") 


kable_styling(gt_tabl1)

```
